# Line endings are content, not formatting, for anything that gets executed.
#
# Development happens on Windows, where the machine-wide core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. That is harmless for source the bundler
# reads, and not harmless at all for scripts/deploy.sh: a shebang line ending
# in CR makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and
# the script dies before a single one of its guard rails runs. Pin the
# executable file types to LF so the checkout matches what the shell and Node
# actually expect, whatever the developer's global git config says.

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
